        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T22:33:55Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): locate the part in a fixture (or the fixture on the part) by mates\n\nLocatePart / LocateFixture (and Locate, either by mover): up to three\nmates - a part face or vertex against a fixture face or vertex - read in\nthe fixture's setup frame and solved as the shop's 3-2-1 (the first face\nmate opposes its normals, the second turns about that normal, every mate\nthen pins the translation still free), then a typed X/Y/Z nudge and a\nturn about the primary mate normal. The part write reuses MoveModel (the\nstock follows) or, in a setup holding the part turned, AlignPartToSetup;\nthe fixture write is MoveFixture with the inverse transform. Every bad\ninput is refused by name at construction; a placement that leaves the\npart inside the fixture warns by name (sampled inside test on the\nfixture mesh law). A moved part stales its setup's ops (undo un-stales);\na moved fixture is re-judged live by the collision gate.\n\nMCP: locate_part, and list_features now lists a fixture's features.\n\nFixes #561\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
