      "message": "fix(app): a located part's stock stays square to the setup\n\nA locate that turned the part back square into the vise turned the box\nstock by the part's whole rotation (MoveModel's rigid follow): a stock\nset square round a turned part ended tilted and under the vise floor,\nand a Face op faced air. A locate now writes through\nMoveModel::locating / AlignPartToSetup::locating: a box or cylinder\nstock square to the setup keeps its orientation and is re-fitted round\nthe part's new place with the allowance it had on each side\n(app::stock_follow). A plain MoveModel keeps its rigid follow. The\ninterpenetration warning also judges the setup's stock against the\nfixture and names it.\n\nPinned by fixture_locate_stock (3 tests) and stock_follow unit tests.\n\nRefs #561\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
