      "message": "fix(ui): a located draft keeps its mates, so the offset and turn can be adjusted after Apply\n\nHand check of #566: after a locate the form cleared its mates, so\nOffset / Turn could only be set before Apply - and once the part sat on\nthe vise floor its bottom face could no longer be picked to start over.\nThe draft now keeps its mates after a landed locate; it reads as\n\"Located. Edit Offset or Turn to adjust\", and an edit re-enables Apply\nlocate as one more undo step solved from the same mates. Stop locating\nends the draft. The first-mate hint says a single face mate sets height\nand tilt only (the jaw mate places X / Y), and the empty hint says the\npicks happen in the viewport.\n\nPinned by locate_tests::the_fixtures_page_locates_* (Offset Z 1 after\nApply lifts the part 1 mm; one undo takes the offset back, the next the\nlocate) and a_refused_draft_says_why_instead_of_offering_apply (a\nlocated draft is not a refusal).\n\nRefs #561\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
